**Project Overview**

This project presents a Big Data analysis pipeline built using Apache Spark and Scala to analyze a real-world LinkedIn job postings dataset. The system processes over 123,000 job records to extract insights about salary trends, job distribution, and labor market patterns. 

The project includes multiple stages such as data preprocessing, distributed analysis using RDDs, SQL-based analytics, and machine learning models for salary prediction. Key findings highlight the strong impact of experience level and geographic location on salaries, while the machine learning models (Random Forest and Gradient Boosted Trees) were used to predict job salaries with improved accuracy over baseline methods. 

Overall, the project demonstrates how big data technologies can be used to handle large-scale datasets, generate meaningful insights, and build predictive models in real-world applications.

